What are Laboratory Monkeys?
Laboratory monkeys are non-human primates (NHPs) serving as critical models in biomedical research due to their genetic, physiological and behavioral similarities to humans. The market primarily utilizes Cynomolgus macaques (Macaca fascicularis) and Rhesus monkeys (Macaca mulatta), which account for over 90% of research specimens. These primates enable scientists to study complex biological processes that can't be replicated in rodents, particularly in neuroscience, immunology and infectious disease research.
